xOTD5485sC94LFGGmP4XozhnpiQD8LjsTIliqEHww`. GitHub Actions secret `GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY` updated. SSH proof with new key returned Gerrit `3.14.1`. Old Gerrit SSH key comment `rebar-ci-gerrit` removed.\n- `/auth-solutions/COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET`: SSM version 2 -> 3 using the documented 48-character openssl/base64 filtering convention. Auth-host Terraform `apply -replace=aws_lambda_function.auth_host` completed (Lambda recreated; API integration updated). The replace dropped the API Gateway invoke permission, causing `/authorize` 500 during smoke; I restored `AllowApiGatewayInvoke` for API `q8mv4bhkmh`. Final smoke: CloudFront `/authorize` returns 302 to Google (location redacted); direct execute-api probe returns 403 as expected. Active SSO sessions are invalidated as expected.\n- `/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key`: SSM version 3 -> 4. New Rebar Bot identity key was added with signed KEY_ADD under identity `594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d`; old key remains registered for historical signatures. New fingerprint `SHA256:oGCqzgfDMpDXRIhYIcmWrYulDr0dVEZLAoJhk2PRxkE`. GitHub Actions secret `REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY` updated. On-box `fetch-secrets.sh` materialized the new private key; review-bot container recreated and health OK.\n- `/rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key`: SSM version 3 -> 4. New public key fingerprint `SHA256:biqEFL9T969c1ADwEKw1KabRGvF4K6qMyxx1ZlpE77o` added to `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` for env `9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65` via Gerrit change 2806; change passed LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and was submitted. After GitHub mirror replication, private key was written to SSM, secrets were rematerialized, opcert was recreated, and MCP was blue/green flipped to live port 8092. MCP `/health` reports `opcert.matched=true`.\n\nRedeploy / health:\n- Secrets-only rematerialization ran on instance `i-00880b2c7f13527c5`: `materialize-deploy-key.sh`, `fetch-secrets.sh`, review-bot recreate, opcert recreate, and MCP blue/green cutover. `rebar-autodeploy.timer` was disabled only during manual recreate windows and is enabled/active again; service idle.\n- Internal health: Gerrit container remained up (not restarted), review-bot `/health` status OK/in_flight 0/queue_depth 0, opcert `/health` OK, MCP live `/health` store present, handshake OK, opcert matched true.\n- External health: Gerrit root HTTP 200, review-bot `/review/health` HTTP 200, MCP `/mcp` HTTP 401 unauthenticated (expected healthy auth boundary), SSO `/authorize` HTTP 302 to Google (redacted).\n\nCarve-outs / deferred items recorded from operator instruction: GitHub OAuth client id/secret and `/auth-solutions/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` were not rotatable by this operator context; `gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key` remains deferred because rotating it breaks clients' known_hosts.\n\nGerrit P1 coordination: no Gerrit restart and no Gerrit git-data mutation were performed; only review flow/replication and non-Gerrit service redeploys were touched.\n","timestamp":1788824441505544001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788771046509100001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ead2e758-435f-4977-b419-b7f8b504ab7b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"097b-de23-bf12-4c38"},{"link_uuid":"cddb34b2-70da-4849-a6ac-249bfeaa18a7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f8aa-c42b-bd8e-468a"}],"description":"## Operator-delegated rotation plan\n\nAlready rotated by operator: `/rebar/prod/anthropic-api-key`, `/rebar/prod/jira-api-token`, `/rebar/prod/gerrit-admin-password`, `/rebar/prod/gerrit-bot-token`, `/rebar/prod/g2p-github-pat`, `/rebar/prod/reviewbot-tickets-pat`, `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot`, `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-codex`, `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude`, `/rebar/prod/mcp-tickets-pat`.\n\nCarve-outs: `github-oauth-client-id`, `github-oauth-client-secret`, and `/auth-solutions/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` are not rotatable by this operator. `/rebar/prod/gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key` is deferred by operator decision because it would break clients' known_hosts pins.\n\n## Precondition: Gerrit review path\n\nBefore any step requiring Gerrit review upload/merge, verify `deserved-rubidium-pussycat` no longer blocks normal `HEAD:refs/for/main` uploads. If the missing-tree receive-pack error remains, do not overwrite production SSM with a key whose public counterpart is unmerged. Complete only non-merge-dependent rotations, leave old trust authoritative for merge-dependent signing/trust, comment the blocked disposition, and do not force-close.\n\nThe merge-dependent step is op-cert trusted-environment YAML. Rebar Bot identity KEY_ADD is a ticket-store operation, but must be signed by the currently valid old Rebar Bot private key before that private key is replaced.\n\n## Scope and sequence\n\n1. `/rebar/prod/github-replication-deploy-key`: generate passphrase-free ed25519; add public key as write deploy key on `navapbc/rebar` using the `rebar-gerrit-replication` convention (unique rotation title if old title still exists); overwrite SSM with private key; redeploy/rematerialize; verify Gerrit→GitHub replication; delete retired GitHub deploy key. Rollback during overlap: restore prior SSM private key and rerun materializer.\n2. `/rebar/prod/ci-gerrit-ssh-key`: generate ed25519; add public key to Gerrit `rebar-ci-bot`; overwrite SSM private key and GitHub Actions `GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY`; verify by real Verify vote-back or SSH `gerrit version` as `rebar-ci-bot`; then delete retired account key. Rollback during overlap: restore old GitHub secret/private key and keep/re-add old pubkey.\n3. `/auth-solutions/COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET`: record current SSM version and confirm prior-value recovery path exists through SSM parameter history/operator-held history before overwrite; generate `openssl rand -base64 36 | tr -d '/+=' | head -c 48`; overwrite SSM; redeploy/recreate auth host Lambda; verify `/authorize` redirects to Google. This invalidates active SSO sessions.\n4. `/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key`: generate ed25519. Before overwriting SSM, materialize current old private key only to a 0600 scratch file, create `env = authorship.sign_authorship(keyop_payload(\"KEY_ADD\", \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", <new-public-key>), key_path=<old-priv-scratch>, principal=\"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\")`, write `dsse.encode(env.payload_type, env.payload, [{\"keyid\": env.signatures[0].keyid, \"sig\": env.signatures[0].sig}])` to a 0600 JSON file, then run `rebar identity key add 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d '<new-public-key>' --signature-file <json>`. After KEY_ADD succeeds, overwrite SSM and GitHub Actions `REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY`. Keep old public key registered. Verify identity shows both keys and a sign/verify smoke test prints no private material.\n5. `/rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key`: only after Gerrit review precondition is green, create a separate worktree from `origin/main`, generate ed25519, run `rebar trusted-env add 9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65 '<new-public-key>' --root <worktree>`, and land that change through Gerrit before overwriting SSM. After merge, overwrite SSM, redeploy/rematerialize `opcert` and `mcp`, and verify opcert container-internal `/health` plus MCP external `GET https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` returns 401 (or container-internal `/health`). Keep old public key registered.\n\n## Safety rules\n\n- No `--force` or equivalent bypass.\n- Never echo, log, commit, or comment secret values; report only names, SSM versions, key ids/titles, and health evidence.\n- Verify each SSM write with `aws ssm get-parameter --name <name> --query Parameter.Version` without `--with-decryption`.\n- Keep scratch key material outside the repo checkout, chmod 0600, remove it after provisioning.\n- Do not restart Gerrit or touch Gerrit git data during the open P1 investigation.\n- Prefer zero-downtime paths: SSM rematerialization via `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh` and validated review-bot/MCP redeploy/blue-green behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Each safe in-scope secret has a generated replacement in SSM and recorded version bump.\n- [x] External trust is updated before consumers switch: GitHub deploy key, Gerrit `rebar-ci-bot` key, signed Rebar Bot KEY_ADD, op-cert trusted-env key merged before op-cert SSM overwrite, and GitHub Actions secrets where applicable.\n- [x] Retired overlap keys are removed only after verification; old Rebar Bot/opcert public keys stay registered.\n- [x] Consumers redeploy/restart with minimal downtime; Gerrit itself is not restarted/touched.\n- [x] Health evidence covers Gerrit, review-bot `/review/health`, replication, MCP external 401 or internal `/health`, op-cert internal `/health`, CI vote-back/SSH proof, and SSO `/authorize` redirect.\n- [x] If Gerrit review upload remains blocked, op-cert rotation is deferred before SSM overwrite and ticket remains open/blocked; no force override.\n- [x] Completion comments name secret names, SSM versions, external registration/deletion evidence, redeploy timing, health checks, carve-outs, and deferred host-key decision, with no secret values.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".rebar/trusted_environments.yaml","reason":"Op-cert public key trust registration must be extended in a separate worktree/Gerrit change so the rotated /rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key remains pinned for env 9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65."},{"path":".tickets-tracker/594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","reason":"Rebar Bot identity keyring is extended by a tracker KEY_ADD event for the new /rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key public key; old key remains for historical signatures."},{"path":"infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh","reason":"Read-only operational dependency: on-box rematerialization path for rebar-bot, opcert, and MCP secrets; no code change intended."},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"Read-only operational dependency: validated secrets-only redeploy path for review-bot and MCP; no code change intended."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","f8aa-c42b-bd8e-468a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"29c1edb0-9bc9-46cf-8ea2-e22a56e235f3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"899f-f964-327c-4c47","ticket_type":"task","title":"Operator: rotate externally anchored secrets","verify_commands":[{"command":"aws ssm get-parameter --region us-east-1 --name <secret-name> --query Parameter.Version --output text","dd_id":"ssm-versions","dd_text":"Each rotated SecureString records a version bump without decrypting values."},{"command":"gh api repos/navapbc/rebar/keys --jq '.[] | {id,title,read_only,created_at}'","dd_id":"github-deploy-key","dd_text":"GitHub mirror deploy key is registered before SSM overwrite and retired only after replication health is proven."},{"command":"curl --fail --silent --show-error --user \"$gerrit_user:$gerrit_password\" https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/a/accounts/rebar-ci-bot/sshkeys","dd_id":"gerrit-ci-key","dd_text":"Gerrit CI account has the new SSH public key during overlap and the retired key removed only after CI vote-back succeeds."},{"command":"curl -fsS https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/login && curl -fsS https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/review/health && curl -fsS https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/health && curl -fsS https://auth.solutions.navateam.com/authorize?return_to=https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com","dd_id":"health","dd_text":"Post-redeploy health checks cover Gerrit, review-bot, MCP, opcert, replication, CI vote-back, and SSO authorize load."}]},"source_event_uuids":["94ade09c-1a07-48c4-a94d-8337eeffde12","d7ca3580-c330-4989-b74a-91e0aae3d4f2","da1ac505-62ae-4867-be46-d07cacad7ecc","a631271d-60b1-4911-ab59-1712bcd657f2","69da66f5-f227-42e8-a473-a9c9f8ac63a8","9c10f899-762c-4da6-a95e-5de274c25c70","42542267-88a4-4f85-9a2f-e4156cd43523","a4e9389e-70dd-4e8a-b948-e0f0ebf6024f","611f3e40-1db1-4fd2-9175-34bd4aed6182","cddb34b2-70da-4849-a6ac-249bfeaa18a7","d2227029-4f86-4334-a6f0-402f59200cc8","4d28bdf5-0384-49a4-8be0-82a43e26c2eb","1cc1d9fe-bcec-466a-8f5a-a6dd86f0a007","29c1edb0-9bc9-46cf-8ea2-e22a56e235f3","2066c58b-a125-4b50-8125-f23511ee25b1"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788827364195756810,"uuid":"0493b9b5-d8b1-400f-9738-15e246af041d"}